**Firebase:**

First, make sure that you have included the Firebase library in your project and initialized it with your project configuration. You can find the instructions on how to set up Firebase in your project here: https://firebase.google.com/docs/web/setup

Once you've set up Firebase, you can get the current user session by calling the `onAuthStateChanged` function within the `firebase.auth()` object:

```javascript
// Initialize Firebase
firebase.initializeApp(config);

// Get the current user session
firebase.auth().onAuthStateChanged((user) => {
  if (user) {
    // User is signed in.
    console.log("User is signed in.");
    // Access the user's ID, display name, email, etc.
    const userID = user.uid;
    const displayName = user.displayName;
    const email = user.email;
    // Use this information as needed
  } else {
    // User is signed out.
    console.log("User is signed out.");
  }
});
```

**Auth0:**

To use Auth0 in your JavaScript application, first include the Auth0 library in your project:

```html
<script src="https://cdn.auth0.com/js/auth0/v10.min.js"></script>
```

Then, initialize Auth0 by creating an instance of the `AuthenticationApi` class and passing your Auth0 domain and client ID:

```javascript
