I have an array as above. This array is set inside the registrations state. The checkMNPStatusAPI is a function
that I call so that it can push another parameter of variable, such as "portInStatus: 1" in each of the data inside
the registrations state. How can I achieve this if I want to push the variable into the registrations state?

response:
 To update the state with a new property for a specific registration object, you can use the functional setState method provided by React instead of directly mutating the state. Here's how you can modify your `checkMNPStatusAPI` function to accomplish this:

```javascript
checkMNPStatusAPI(phoneNo, index) {
  const updatedRegistrations = [...this.state.registrations]; // create a copy of the registrations array
  fetch(api.checkPortInStatus(user.getProductCode(), phoneNo), {
    headers: new Headers({ "Authorization": "Bearer " + user.getAccessToken() }),
    method: 'GET'
  })
    .then(response => response.json())
    .then(rjson => {
      updatedRegistrations[index].mnpStatus = rjson.status; // update the mnpStatus of the specific registration object
      this.setState({ registrations: updatedRegistrations }); // set the updated state
    })
    .catch(error => console.error('Error:', error));
}
```

This way, when the API call completes successfully and updates the `mnpStatus`, the component's state will be updated with the new data, causing any subscribing components to re-render with the latest information.
